; DOMAIN: homological-algebra/spectral-sequences [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: A (cohomological) spectral sequence is a sequence of bigraded pages {E_r^{p,q}, d_r} with differentials d_r of bidegree (r, 1-r) satisfying d_r^2=0, where each page is the cohomology of the previous: E_{r+1} = H(E_r, d_r). A filtered (co)chain complex, or a double complex, gives rise to a spectral sequence whose E_2 page is a computable homology-of-homology; if the filtration is bounded/regular the sequence converges (E_infinity), and E_infinity^{p,q} is the associated graded of a filtration on the target (co)homology H^{p+q}. Key instances: the Serre spectral sequence of a fibration F->E->B with E_2^{p,q}=H^p(B; H^q(F)) => H^{p+q}(E); the Grothendieck spectral sequence for a composite of derived functors R^p F (R^q G) => R^{p+q}(F.G); the Hochschild-Serre spectral sequence H^p(G/N; H^q(N;M)) => H^{p+q}(G;M) for a normal subgroup; the Lyndon/Leray sequences. An exact couple (D,E,i,j,k) generates a spectral sequence by iterated derivation, the derived couple giving successive pages.
; Structure: (E_{r+1}=H(E_r,d_r), d_r bidegree (r,1-r), d_r^2=0) (E_2 computable = homology-of-homology of filtered/double complex) (bounded filtration => convergence E_infinity = associated graded of H^{p+q}) (Serre: E_2^{p,q}=H^p(B;H^q(F)) => H^{p+q}(E)) (Grothendieck: R^pF(R^qG) => R^{p+q}(FG)) (Hochschild-Serre: H^p(G/N;H^q(N;M)) => H^{p+q}(G;M)) (exact couple + derived couple generates the pages).
; Result: spectral sequences are the systematic bookkeeping device that computes an associated graded of a (co)homology by successive approximations, turning filtrations, fibrations, and composite derived functors into tractable E_2-inputs plus a convergence process.
; Bridge: genesis_ext_tor (Grothendieck spectral sequence composes derived functors; the E_2 page is built from Ext/Tor of the intermediate derived functors) + genesis_group_cohomology (Hochschild-Serre spectral sequence H^p(G/N;H^q(N;M)) => H^{p+q}(G;M) computes group cohomology from a normal subgroup and quotient) + genesis_homology (a filtered chain complex or double complex yields a spectral sequence converging to its total homology; E_infinity = associated graded) + genesis_de_rham (the filtration of the de Rham/Cech double complex gives the spectral sequences relating de Rham, Cech, and singular cohomology).
(= (page $E $r) (if (= $r 2) (E2-input $E) (homology (page $E (pred $r)) (differential $r))))
(= (differential-bidegree $r) (tuple $r (minus 1 $r)))
(= (converges $E $H) (= (E-infinity $E) (associated-graded (filtration $H))))
(= (serre-ss $F $E $B) (=> (E2 (cohomology $B (cohomology $F))) (cohomology $E)))
(= (grothendieck-ss $F $G) (=> (E2 (derived $F (derived $G))) (derived (compose $F $G))))
(= (hochschild-serre $G $N $M) (=> (E2 (group-cohomology (quotient $G $N) (group-cohomology $N $M))) (group-cohomology $G $M)))
(= (spectral-sequence-of $couple) (iterate derived-couple $couple))